SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Aimilianos\, Angeria
LOCATION:Angeria\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Angeria\, the farming village on the road to Paliochori\, celebrates its Agios Aimilianos with vespers at 20:00 on 17 July followed by a courtyard glenti with violin and laouto players from the island\, and liturgy at 07:00 next morning. A canteen sells local food and drink\, so come hungry\; it's a low-key\, mostly local affair — a good pick if you find the Adamas feasts too busy.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#angeria-panigiri-of-agios-aimilianos-angeria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#angeria-panigiri-of-agios-aimilianos-angeria
